      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>Rabbi Zalman Schachter-Shalomi, z”l, included his translation of Rabbi Yitsḥak Luria’s prayer “<tei:hi rend="italic">Hareni Moḥel</tei:hi>” (I hereby forgive) in his <tei:hi rend="italic">Siddur Tehillat Hashem Yidaber Pi</tei:hi> (2009). To the best of my ability, I have set his translation side-by-side with a transcription of the vocalized text of the prayer.</tei:p>
        <tei:p>The prayer by the ARI z”l was first published in Ḥayim Vital’s <tei:hi rend="italic">Pri Ets Ḥayyim, Shaar Kriyat Shema al Hamitah, Pereq 2</tei:hi> (פרי עץ חיים, שער קריאת שמע שעל המיטה, פרק ב), and based on the statement of Reish Lakish in the Bavli Pesachim 66b and the practice of Mar Zutra attested in the Bavli Megillah 28a:</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_16104_notes"/>
